WEBVTT

1

00:00:19.500 --> 00:00:22.750

Go, Eren!



2

00:00:30.540 --> 00:00:32.950

In the year 850,



3

00:00:32.950 --> 00:00:38.370

humanity successfully took back land

from the Titans for the very first time.



4

00:00:39.620 --> 00:00:42.000

At great cost.



5

00:00:44.500 --> 00:00:46.790

All of you here are hereby accepted



6

00:00:46.790 --> 00:00:50.080

as new members

of the Scout Regiment!



7

00:00:50.080 --> 00:00:52.450

<i>This </i>is a genuine salute!



8

00:00:52.450 --> 00:00:54.330

Give your hearts!



9

00:00:55.750 --> 00:00:57.160

Yes, Sir!



10

00:01:00.950 --> 00:01:03.830

You've done well to endure your fear.



11

00:01:03.830 --> 00:01:06.660

You're all brave soldiers.



12

00:01:06.660 --> 00:01:08.830

I respect you from the bottom of my heart.



13

00:01:10.040 --> 00:01:15.410

One month later,

the Scout Regiment, led by Erwin Smith,



14

00:01:15.410 --> 00:01:19.450

left Calaneth District to

establish a route to Shiganshina,



15

00:01:19.450 --> 00:01:23.540

which is believed to

house a secret of the Titans.



16

00:01:28.540 --> 00:01:32.910

Now commencing the

57th Exterior Scouting Mission!



17

00:01:32.910 --> 00:01:35.040

Move out!



18

00:02:05.830 --> 00:02:11.500

<i>I won't let your deaths be meaningless</i>



19

00:02:11.500 --> 00:02:17.620

<i>even if I'm the last one standing</i>



20

00:02:22.620 --> 00:02:26.500

<i>In both hands, Gloria</i>



21

00:02:26.500 --> 00:02:28.500

<i>What sings is Sieg</i>



22

00:02:28.500 --> 00:02:33.700

<i>On my back, Flügel der Freiheit</i>



23

00:02:34.620 --> 00:02:40.540

<i>Clenched determination to my left chest</i>



24

00:02:40.540 --> 00:02:45.910

<i>What slashes across is Linie der Torheit</i>



25

00:02:46.580 --> 00:02:49.160

<i>Soaring across the azure skies</i>



26

00:02:49.160 --> 00:02:53.700

<i>Flügel der Freiheit</i>



27

00:03:07.450 --> 00:03:12.330

"Female Titan"

"The 57th Exterior Scouting Mission, Part 1"



28

00:03:32.450 --> 00:03:35.120

10-meter Titan ahead,

approaching from the left!



29

00:03:35.120 --> 00:03:38.700

I'm extremely curious to

know what's inside its stomach!



30

00:03:38.700 --> 00:03:41.500

But I'll let the support squad handle it!



31

00:03:44.620 --> 00:03:47.620

Damn! Not deep enough!



32

00:03:47.620 --> 00:03:49.450

Defend the ranks!



33

00:03:53.500 --> 00:03:55.000

Don't falter!



34

00:03:55.000 --> 00:03:57.790

Leave it to the support squad!

Keep moving!



35

00:03:59.450 --> 00:04:00.870

Forward!



36

00:04:01.120 --> 00:04:03.540

Forward!



37

00:04:08.500 --> 00:04:11.620

The support squad will only

cover us until we're through the old city.



38

00:04:11.620 --> 00:04:15.250

Everything beyond

that is wholly Titan territory.



39

00:04:15.250 --> 00:04:16.870

From then on,



40

00:04:16.870 --> 00:04:21.330

we'll have to rely on Commander

Erwin's long-range scouting formation.



41

00:04:21.330 --> 00:04:24.500

Our special operations

squad will be positioned here.



42

00:04:26.540 --> 00:04:27.950

Mr. Oruo!



43

00:04:27.950 --> 00:04:31.950

Do you think they--my classmates--

can beat the Titans in a fight?



44

00:04:31.950 --> 00:04:36.000

Huh? What the hell did you just

spend this last month doing?!



45

00:04:37.500 --> 00:04:39.330

Listen, kid!



46

00:04:39.330 --> 00:04:42.330

Outside scouting missions

are about fighting Titans



47

00:04:42.330 --> 00:04:44.750

as little as possi--



48

00:04:52.200 --> 00:04:55.120

Assume long-range scouting formation!



49

00:04:56.540 --> 00:04:58.910

See you later, Armin.



50

00:04:58.910 --> 00:05:02.080

Don't wet your pants

if you run into a Titan!



51

00:05:02.080 --> 00:05:04.450

Right! Likewise to you!



52

00:05:11.700 --> 00:05:14.160

"Row 3-3: Signaling"

This formation is a forward-facing semicircle,



53

00:05:14.160 --> 00:05:15.200

with soldiers positioned



54

00:05:15.200 --> 00:05:17.040

"Row 5, Center: Standby"

far from each other at equal intervals



55

00:05:17.040 --> 00:05:19.870

"Row 2-5: Signaling"

yet still within clear sight on all sides.



56

00:05:19.870 --> 00:05:20.870

Extend the spotting



57

00:05:20.870 --> 00:05:23.580

"Row 3-4: Signaling"

and signaling range as far as possible!



58

00:05:23.580 --> 00:05:25.910

"Row 2-4: Signaling"



59

00:05:49.700 --> 00:05:52.410

It's okay. Stay calm.



60

00:05:56.580 --> 00:06:01.620

The soldiers in the front-row spotting

squads will encounter most of the Titans.



61

00:06:02.120 --> 00:06:03.830

"Row 1-8: Spotting"



62

00:06:07.580 --> 00:06:10.290

As soon as they spot a Titan



63

00:06:10.290 --> 00:06:12.580

they'll fire a red smoke signal.



64

00:06:15.200 --> 00:06:19.790

Soldiers who see this signal

will then signal others similarly.



65

00:06:20.910 --> 00:06:22.700

"Row 2, Center: Command"



66

00:06:23.290 --> 00:06:26.950

Once the commander has

learned of the Titan's position,



67

00:06:26.950 --> 00:06:29.370

he'll fire a green signal



68

00:06:30.120 --> 00:06:33.700

and reroute the

entire platoon around it.



69

00:06:35.200 --> 00:06:40.000

This will allow the platoon

to proceed toward its destination



70

00:06:40.000 --> 00:06:42.660

while avoiding the Titans entirely.



71

00:06:42.660 --> 00:06:44.500

"Row 2-3: Signaling"



72

00:06:44.910 --> 00:06:49.410

However, as the terrain and other

obstacles could delay their detection,



73

00:06:49.410 --> 00:06:52.700

we <i>may </i>encounter

Titans inside the formation.



74

00:07:00.000 --> 00:07:03.120

R-Red... Red signal...!



75

00:07:06.450 --> 00:07:09.160

Braus! Over here!



76

00:07:10.500 --> 00:07:13.120

Damn! The spotters missed one!



77

00:07:13.120 --> 00:07:14.950

Let's lure it this way!



78

00:07:14.950 --> 00:07:17.500

Braus! Run toward us!



79

00:07:27.660 --> 00:07:29.500

Break away! I'll handle this!



80

00:07:29.500 --> 00:07:30.910

Yes, Sir!



81

00:07:48.950 --> 00:07:50.250

Sir!



82

00:07:50.250 --> 00:07:53.660

It's conked out!

Return to your position!



83

00:07:58.370 --> 00:08:00.370

Something's not right...



84

00:08:00.370 --> 00:08:04.910

It's been a while since the last red signal,

yet the formation's in disarray.



85

00:08:04.910 --> 00:08:06.750

Could it be...?



86

00:08:07.080 --> 00:08:11.540

Keep in mind, this strategy

will only work with "Normals,"



87

00:08:11.540 --> 00:08:14.040

Titans with predictable behavior.



88

00:08:16.580 --> 00:08:18.750

A black smoke signal?!



89

00:08:18.750 --> 00:08:20.540

It's ignoring everyone nearby



90

00:08:20.540 --> 00:08:22.870

and heading straight for

the center of the formation?!



91

00:08:23.750 --> 00:08:27.330

No doubt about it! It's...



92

00:08:27.330 --> 00:08:28.950

...an Abnormal!



93

00:08:30.410 --> 00:08:35.000

Only when dealing with unpredictable

Abnormals is combat necessary!



94

00:08:35.000 --> 00:08:37.410

Damn! No choice but to fight!



95

00:08:37.410 --> 00:08:39.870

Cis! You go for its nape!



96

00:08:39.870 --> 00:08:41.290

I'll stop it in its tracks!



97

00:08:41.290 --> 00:08:42.700

Understood!



98

00:08:44.580 --> 00:08:47.750

An ODM battle on level ground

puts us at a clear disadvantage.



99

00:08:47.750 --> 00:08:50.080

Our chances of success are incredibly low,



100

00:08:50.080 --> 00:08:53.750

but we can't afford to

let it wreck our formation!



101

00:08:53.750 --> 00:08:56.410

Arlelt's that way, as I recall.



102

00:08:56.410 --> 00:08:59.410

I can't let a rookie face this thing!



103

00:08:59.870 --> 00:09:01.660

I'm taking it out here!



104

00:09:09.450 --> 00:09:11.080

Now, Cis!



105

00:09:17.450 --> 00:09:20.250

Way to go, Section Commander Ness!



106

00:09:22.410 --> 00:09:23.830

Got it!



107

00:09:25.540 --> 00:09:28.660

You came! You're my horse, all right!



108

00:09:29.620 --> 00:09:32.410

I love ya, Charrette!



109

00:09:40.410 --> 00:09:44.370

Another one?! What are

the right wing spotters doing?!



110

00:09:44.370 --> 00:09:48.910

It must be an Abnormal too.

It's ignoring everyone on its way here.



111

00:09:48.910 --> 00:09:50.750

Ugh, all right...



112

00:09:51.580 --> 00:09:53.410

Let's do it again, Cis!



113

00:09:53.410 --> 00:09:54.830

Yes, Sir!



114

00:09:55.290 --> 00:09:59.290

Man, two in a row...

Talk about unlucky.



115

00:09:59.290 --> 00:10:02.040

Plus, this one looks

to be 14-meters high.



116

00:10:02.040 --> 00:10:04.500

This is gonna be tough.



117

00:10:13.370 --> 00:10:15.870

What the...! It's way too fast!



118

00:10:15.870 --> 00:10:17.830

Don't let it go for Arlelt!



119

00:10:17.830 --> 00:10:19.080

Cis!



120

00:10:19.080 --> 00:10:20.500

Yes, Sir!



121

00:10:54.450 --> 00:10:57.120

No! This one's different!



122

00:10:57.120 --> 00:11:00.410

This isn't an Abnormal...

It has intelligence!



123

00:11:00.410 --> 00:11:03.910

It's just like the Armored Titan,

the Colossal Titan, and Eren!



124

00:11:03.910 --> 00:11:07.000

It's a human clad in a Titan body!



125

00:11:07.000 --> 00:11:09.750

B-But who?! Why?!



126

00:11:09.750 --> 00:11:11.290

This is bad! What do I do?!



127

00:11:11.290 --> 00:11:13.790

It's going to kill me too!



128

00:11:15.040 --> 00:11:17.580

Go! Run for it!



129

00:11:24.250 --> 00:11:26.080

What is its--



130

00:11:27.950 --> 00:11:30.250

No, what is <i>their</i>...



131

00:11:33.500 --> 00:11:35.370

...goal?!



132

00:11:49.830 --> 00:11:52.580

S-Someone, let the others know...



133

00:11:52.580 --> 00:11:57.330

The right wing spotting squads...

are almost entirely wiped out...



134

00:11:57.330 --> 00:12:02.660

A female-looking Titan...

brought a horde of Titans with her...



135

00:12:03.540 --> 00:12:06.450

Is... anyone left...?



136

00:13:04.250 --> 00:13:07.040

It... didn't kill me?



137

00:13:07.040 --> 00:13:08.910

What just happened?



138

00:13:09.410 --> 00:13:11.750

It pinched my hood and...



139

00:13:11.750 --> 00:13:13.870

My face?



140

00:13:13.870 --> 00:13:16.790

It checked my face?



141

00:13:16.790 --> 00:13:18.200

Armin!



142

00:13:19.040 --> 00:13:20.450

Reiner!



143

00:13:20.790 --> 00:13:23.330

Hey, can you stand?!



144

00:13:23.330 --> 00:13:27.790

There's no surviving outside

the wall without a horse, you know!



145

00:13:27.790 --> 00:13:28.790

Hurry!



146

00:13:28.790 --> 00:13:30.200

Mm!



147

00:13:32.120 --> 00:13:34.700

I saw the Abnormal smoke signal.



148

00:13:34.700 --> 00:13:37.160

Is it that one with the nice butt?



149

00:13:37.160 --> 00:13:41.200

It's not an Abnormal!

It's a person clad in a Titan body!



150

00:13:41.200 --> 00:13:42.620

What?!



151

00:13:43.580 --> 00:13:46.450

Hold on! We need to

fire a smoke signal first!



152

00:13:46.450 --> 00:13:50.080

H-Hurry. We have to let them know...



153

00:13:50.080 --> 00:13:51.580

...there's an emergency--



154

00:13:52.450 --> 00:13:53.830

Wait.



155

00:13:53.830 --> 00:13:55.750

It looks like Jean fired for us.



156

00:13:58.790 --> 00:14:00.660

From the right wing?!



157

00:14:00.660 --> 00:14:03.950

They've suffered too severe of

an attack to continue the operation?!



158

00:14:03.950 --> 00:14:06.790

Apparently part of the

right wing's been wiped out!



159

00:14:06.790 --> 00:14:10.870

A whole horde of Titans showed up!

I dunno how it happened, though!



160

00:14:10.870 --> 00:14:13.120

A bunch of 'em are fast, too!



161

00:14:13.120 --> 00:14:17.410

We're holding them off for now,

but no one's on spotting duty now!



162

00:14:17.410 --> 00:14:21.330

This is a serious setback; if we're

not careful we could <i>all </i>get wiped out!



163

00:14:21.330 --> 00:14:23.950

That's the direction she came from...



164

00:14:23.950 --> 00:14:25.370

Could it be?



165

00:14:25.370 --> 00:14:27.910

Did <i>she </i>lead the Titans here?!



166

00:14:27.910 --> 00:14:29.870

She?



167

00:14:29.870 --> 00:14:32.620

What's a Titan doing <i>there</i>?!



168

00:14:32.620 --> 00:14:33.950

Is it an Abnormal?!



169

00:14:33.950 --> 00:14:39.790

No, it's a human clad in a Titan body.



170

00:14:39.790 --> 00:14:42.290

A human who can

do the same thing as Eren.



171

00:14:42.290 --> 00:14:43.910

What?!



172

00:14:43.910 --> 00:14:46.580

What makes you think that, Armin?



173

00:14:47.450 --> 00:14:50.450

"Eating" is all that Titans do.



174

00:14:50.450 --> 00:14:55.410

This results in death of course,

but "killing" isn't their actual goal.



175

00:14:55.410 --> 00:15:00.790

But as soon as more experienced

soldiers went for her vital spot,



176

00:15:00.790 --> 00:15:03.160

she crushed and swatted them down.



177

00:15:03.160 --> 00:15:06.950

And she didn't do it to eat them...

she did it to kill them.



178

00:15:06.950 --> 00:15:10.000

She's unlike any other Titan in that regard.



179

00:15:10.000 --> 00:15:13.750

<i>She </i>must've been the one

who brought the hordes of Titans



180

00:15:13.750 --> 00:15:18.000

when the Colossal and Armored

Titans destroyed the walls.



181

00:15:18.000 --> 00:15:22.200

Meaning she's had the consistent

goal of attacking humankind.



182

00:15:23.160 --> 00:15:25.410

Or, actually...



183

00:15:25.410 --> 00:15:28.540

I think she might be searching for someone.



184

00:15:28.540 --> 00:15:32.160

If so, who?



185

00:15:32.160 --> 00:15:34.250

Could it be Eren?!



186

00:15:34.250 --> 00:15:36.000

Eren?



187

00:15:36.000 --> 00:15:41.250

Eren's with the Levi Squad.

They're in charge of the right wing.



188

00:15:41.250 --> 00:15:43.200

Right wing?



189

00:15:43.200 --> 00:15:48.160

My copy of the plan had

them in the rear of the left wing.



190

00:15:48.160 --> 00:15:53.500

My copy placed them

at the front of the right wing...



191

00:15:53.500 --> 00:15:56.910

Wait, there's no way they'd

be put on the front lines like that.



192

00:15:56.910 --> 00:15:59.790

Then where <i>are </i>they?



193

00:15:59.790 --> 00:16:04.040

The safest place in

this formation, I'd assume.



194

00:16:04.040 --> 00:16:05.540

Which would be...



195

00:16:05.540 --> 00:16:08.500

...the rear of the center rank.



196

00:16:08.500 --> 00:16:09.870

Armin!



197

00:16:09.870 --> 00:16:12.540

This is no time to get lost in thought!



198

00:16:12.540 --> 00:16:16.330

Smoke signals aren't enough to

explain how much of a threat she poses!



199

00:16:16.330 --> 00:16:18.700

At this rate, she'll take

out the command squad too.



200

00:16:18.700 --> 00:16:21.910

And if that happens, the formation

falls apart and we <i>all </i>die!



201

00:16:21.910 --> 00:16:23.660

What are you suggesting?



202

00:16:23.660 --> 00:16:28.540

I'm suggesting that from this distance

we might still be able to distract her.



203

00:16:28.540 --> 00:16:32.250

We can buy some time

for everyone to retreat.



204

00:16:32.250 --> 00:16:35.790

Maybe, anyway...



205

00:16:37.790 --> 00:16:40.580

She really does have intelligence.



206

00:16:40.580 --> 00:16:44.080

From her point of view,

we're literally just like insects.



207

00:16:44.080 --> 00:16:46.540

All it takes is one swipe to kill us.



208

00:16:46.540 --> 00:16:48.160

You don't say...



209

00:16:49.080 --> 00:16:51.080

That's some scary stuff.



210

00:16:51.080 --> 00:16:54.080

Are you really Jean?



211

00:16:54.080 --> 00:16:58.790

The Jean I know only

ever cares about himself.



212

00:16:58.790 --> 00:17:00.620

That's rude.



213

00:17:02.910 --> 00:17:05.910

I just don't want to

meet a disappointing end



214

00:17:05.910 --> 00:17:10.700

as a bunch of burnt bones

that you can't even tell are mine.



215

00:17:10.700 --> 00:17:16.410

I... I know what needs to be done now!



216

00:17:16.410 --> 00:17:19.540

Plus, we <i>chose </i>to take this job!



217

00:17:19.540 --> 00:17:20.950

Help me!



218

00:17:26.450 --> 00:17:31.290

Put your hoods on! All the way,

so she can't see your face!



219

00:17:31.290 --> 00:17:36.080

Because she can't risk killing

us if she can't tell who we are!



220

00:17:36.080 --> 00:17:37.620

I get it.



221

00:17:37.620 --> 00:17:41.410

She can't risk killing

anyone who might be Eren.



222

00:17:41.410 --> 00:17:43.450

Now <i>that's </i>a relief to know.



223

00:17:43.450 --> 00:17:47.450

Here's hoping she's

got bad eyesight too!



224

00:17:47.450 --> 00:17:48.660

Armin...



225

00:17:48.660 --> 00:17:53.290

The way you always clung so

close to Eren used to creep me out,



226

00:17:53.290 --> 00:17:55.120

but I always knew I could count on you.



227

00:17:55.120 --> 00:17:58.290

Huh? Oh, thanks.



228

00:17:58.290 --> 00:18:01.290

But that's mean, thinking I'm creepy...



229

00:18:15.870 --> 00:18:18.870

She's a lot slower than

when she came from that way.



230

00:18:18.870 --> 00:18:20.790

Is she tired?



231

00:18:20.790 --> 00:18:23.620

If she takes off at that

speed again we'll be too late!



232

00:18:23.620 --> 00:18:27.080

We have to do it now!

We have to act now, or else...!



233

00:18:32.700 --> 00:18:36.080

All right, guys.

Do it like we just discussed.



234

00:18:36.080 --> 00:18:38.450

Distract her for as long as possible



235

00:18:38.450 --> 00:18:40.870

so the platoon can retreat!



236

00:18:40.870 --> 00:18:44.040

We hafta keep her here as long as we can!



237

00:18:44.040 --> 00:18:47.500

Cutting her heel tendons

should be more than enough.



238

00:18:47.500 --> 00:18:51.910

But don't do anything crazy.

We don't need to kill her!



239

00:18:51.910 --> 00:18:55.040

She's aware of the

vital spot on her nape.



240

00:18:55.040 --> 00:18:57.500

She's completely different

from the other Titans.



241

00:18:57.500 --> 00:18:59.450

Killing her is probably out of the question.



242

00:18:59.450 --> 00:19:04.080

At least for ordinary people, anyway.



243

00:19:07.200 --> 00:19:10.700

But maybe those two could...!



244

00:19:52.120 --> 00:19:53.540

Armin!



245

00:19:55.250 --> 00:19:58.950

This one's <i>way </i>more athletic

than the other ones!



246

00:19:58.950 --> 00:20:01.160

Damn! We were...



247

00:20:01.160 --> 00:20:03.250

We were too naïve!



248

00:20:08.200 --> 00:20:10.290

She's protecting her nape?!



249

00:20:10.290 --> 00:20:11.700

Jean!



250

00:20:12.620 --> 00:20:15.200

Damn! There's no escape now!



251

00:20:15.200 --> 00:20:19.080

I'm dead! She's gonna

grab my wire and finish me!



252

00:20:22.200 --> 00:20:26.580

Jean! Avenge that suicidal maniac!



253

00:20:27.750 --> 00:20:29.160

Armin?



254

00:20:29.870 --> 00:20:31.830

She stopped?



255

00:20:31.830 --> 00:20:34.620

It was her! She killed him!



256

00:20:34.620 --> 00:20:37.290

That maniac finally got himself killed,

as part of the right wing!



257

00:20:37.290 --> 00:20:39.870

She killed him!



258

00:20:45.290 --> 00:20:47.160

What's going on?!



259

00:20:47.950 --> 00:20:52.290

Did he hit his head and get confused?!

This is the worst possible time...!



260

00:20:53.620 --> 00:20:55.500

Reiner...



261

00:20:55.500 --> 00:20:58.750

<i>She </i>crushed my friend!



262

00:20:58.750 --> 00:21:02.040

I saw him stuck to the bottom of her foot!



263

00:21:04.080 --> 00:21:06.330

He's going straight for the nape?!



264

00:21:06.330 --> 00:21:11.000

No, he can do it! Now's his chance,

while she's focused on Armin!



265

00:21:18.330 --> 00:21:20.330

H-Hey...



266

00:21:33.250 --> 00:21:34.870

H-Hey!



267

00:21:34.870 --> 00:21:37.330

Reiner... You...



268

00:21:53.870 --> 00:21:56.290

Ol' Reiner actually did it...!



269

00:21:56.290 --> 00:21:58.660

Mikasa stole so much

of the spotlight that I forgot



270

00:21:58.660 --> 00:22:02.660

that he's extremely skilled

and dependable too!



271

00:22:02.660 --> 00:22:07.000

I'd say we bought enough time!

Now let's get away from her, quick!



272

00:22:07.000 --> 00:22:11.040

She doesn't eat people!

I don't think she'll follow us!



273

00:22:19.120 --> 00:22:24.450

Look! The giant wench is running

home with her tail between her legs!



274

00:22:24.450 --> 00:22:26.790

Huh? Oh no...



275

00:22:26.790 --> 00:22:28.000

Why?



276

00:22:28.000 --> 00:22:30.580

The rear of the center rank is that way...



277

00:22:30.580 --> 00:22:34.450

Is she heading for Eren?!



278

00:22:52.540 --> 00:22:57.790

<i>If, by chance, I'm not me</i>



279

00:22:57.790 --> 00:23:03.040

<i>then who's to say that you're you?</i>



280

00:23:03.040 --> 00:23:08.330

<i>Can you pick up the pieces of your heart</i>



281

00:23:08.330 --> 00:23:13.450

<i>that fell apart like a broken sand castle?</i>



282

00:23:13.450 --> 00:23:18.450

<i>The voice of someone calling out</i>



283

00:23:18.450 --> 00:23:22.540

<i>changed into ringing in my ears</i>



284

00:23:22.540 --> 00:23:27.700

<i>It's as if time has stopped</i>



285

00:23:27.700 --> 00:23:30.500

<i>Now wake up</i>



286

00:23:30.500 --> 00:23:35.790

<i>I made my way out of the deep darkness</i>



287

00:23:35.790 --> 00:23:41.040

<i>I fled like a swift wind</i>



288

00:23:41.040 --> 00:23:48.540

<i>We used to be like living corpses,</i>



289

00:23:48.540 --> 00:23:50.580

<i>but now we head beyond the walls</i>



290

00:23:50.580 --> 00:23:52.620

<i>Let's meet again</i>



291

00:23:52.620 --> 00:23:57.450

<i>in a place not on any map</i>



292

00:24:09.790 --> 00:24:12.040

"You monster!"



293

00:24:12.040 --> 00:24:17.540

Not even the highly trained Scout

Regiment can stop the Female Titan.



294

00:24:17.540 --> 00:24:20.290

Eventually, inside a forest of giant trees,



295

00:24:20.290 --> 00:24:21.910

the monster finally catches sight of Eren.



296

00:24:21.910 --> 00:24:23.450

"Forest of Giant Trees"

"The 57th Exterior Scouting Mission, Part 2"

